@startuml j5-staff-reply
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J5 A staff reply reaches the chat
actor "Staff" as Staff <<person>>
box "In the staff browser"
participant "Staff page\n(staff/staff.js,\nsync.js)" as SP <<container>>
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core <<component>>
end box
box "Vercel functions"
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix <<container>>
participant "api/messages.js" as Msg <<container>>
end box
database "Postgres\n(Neon)" as Store <<store>>
box "In the patient's browser"
participant "Patient chat\n(chat.js, sync.js,\nshared.js)" as Chat <<container>>
end box
actor "Patient" as Patient <<person>>

== At the desk ==
Staff -> SP : opens a ticket,\ntypes in the reply\nbox and presses\n"Send reply"
SP -> Core : FD.replyToTicket\n(ticket, text)
Core --> SP : the reply is on the ticket\nin the staff browser;\n"Needs human" or "Urgent"\nbecomes "Answered"
SP --> Staff : "Sent. The patient sees\nit in their chat."
SP -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets\n(the ticket, with\nthe desk code)
Tix -> Store : merged into the row\nin the table tickets
note left of Store : every staff reply is kept;\nthe status further along wins
== In the patient's chat ==
loop every 10 s while the chat is open
  Chat -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets\n?patient=<id> (with\nthis browser's key)
  Tix -> Store : read this patient's tickets
  Tix --> Chat : the ticket with\nthe staff reply
end
Chat -> Chat : sync.js merges it into\nthis browser's tickets;\nchat.js redraws
Chat --> Patient : the reply, headed\n"From the clinic team"
Chat -> Msg : shared.js: POST /api/messages\n(the staff reply, once)
Msg -> Store : a row in the\ntable messages
@enduml
